1 DNS64 proxy
## 3.1 DNS64 proxy

For each DNS query, we use "dns64\_proxy\_t" to trace the session, it will forward the query to NS6 server first, and repeat the query to NS6 server later. If get response from NS6 server, it will forward it to client, if get response from NS4 server, it will construct a AAAA record from the response, and send the synthesis one to client.

![](data:image/x-wmf;base64...)

Figure 3-1 DNS64 architechture

#define DNS64\_MODE\_4A 0

#define DNS64\_MODE\_A 1

typedef \_dns64\_proxy {

int mode; /\* DNS64\_MODE\_4A, DNS64\_MODE\_A\*/

void \*client\_conn;

void \*server\_conn6;

void \*server\_conn4;

int ns6\_fail;

int ns4\_fail;

void \*vs\_p;

dns\_req\_t \*request\_pending;

click\_callout\_t request\_pending\_callout;

}dns64\_proxy\_t;

2 DNS64 parser
## 3.2 DNS64 parser

Current data structure:

dns\_header\_t;

dns\_answer\_t;

#define DNS\_RR\_TYPE\_A 1

#define DNS\_RR\_TYPE\_4A 28

Data structure of struct \_dns\_req and struct \_dns\_resp:

![](data:image/x-wmf;base64...)

Figure 3-2 dns\_section\_t

/\* Used for DNS64 parser.\*/

typedef \_dns\_section\_info {

char \*name\_p;

uint16\_t name\_len;

uint16\_t type;

uint16\_t class;

}dns\_section\_info\_t;

typedef \_dns\_question {

char type[2];

char class[2];

}dns\_question\_t;

typedef \_dns\_req {

dns\_header\_t \*dns\_header\_p;

dns\_section\_info\_t qd;

struct mbuf \*packet;

}dns\_req\_t;

typedef \_dns\_resp {

dns\_header\_t \*dns\_header\_p;

dns\_section\_info\_t qd;

dns\_section\_info\_t an[MAX\_DNS\_REC];

struct mbuf \*packet;

}dns\_resp\_t;

3 DNS64 dynamic NAT table
## 3.3 DNS64 dynamic NAT table

DNS64 use a dynamic nat table to trace the mapping rules of AAAA -> A, the nat entry could be indexed in two way:

1. NAT64 : IPv4 traffic use destination address to index it in linear manner.
2. DNS64 : Use AAAA record to index it by hash-tree.

Ilegal IPv4 address in IP region will be set reserved.

![](data:image/x-wmf;base64...)

Figure 3-3 Dynamic NAT table

NAT entry allocate algorithm:

offset = hash\_1 (AAAA) "or" hash\_2 (AAAA) "or" hash\_3(AAAA)" or " any null bucket.

A = A\_array[offset];

/\* Used for dynamic nat table. \*/

typedef \_dns64\_nat\_entry {

int last\_ticks; /\* Updated by new connection, used for nat entry timeout.\*/

uint32\_t ip;

struct in6\_addr ip6;

}dns64\_nat\_entry\_t;

#define DNS64\_HASH\_SIZE (64 \* 1024)

#define DNS64\_HASH\_SLOT 1024

typedef \_dns64\_ipregion {

uint32\_t base;

uint32\_t end;

uint32\_t num;

struct mtx allocation\_lock;

uint32\_t last\_allocation\_offset\_mp[ATCP\_MAXTHREADS];

dns64\_nat\_entry\_t \*\*nat\_table;

/\* Hash table for dns64\_nat\_entry\_t \*/

hash\_t \*hash\_table;

struct mtx hash\_table\_lock[DNS64\_HASH\_SLOT];

}

